  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workshop Strategic Marine Spatial Plan Offshore Wind Colombia in collaboration with NCEA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Mines and Energy (MME) of Colombia leads the development of the offshore wind and green hydrogen sectors in Colombia. Under the CERF programme and within the framework of a bilateral Memorandum of Understanding, the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands collaborates with MME to support Colombia&#x2019;s renewable energy transition.In partnership with the Netherlands Commission for Environmental Assessment (NCEA), the project addresses social and environmental considerations related to offshore wind development to promote a just transition. The activity focuses on co-creating a scoping report outlining the proposed process for developing a strategic marine spatial plan. This report is intended to inform decision-makers, support the formal mandate for the planning process, and provide a basis for engaging technical expertise to guide its implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
